--- a/docs/en/dev/backend/01-nvidia-target-info.md
+++ b/docs/en/dev/backend/01-nvidia-target-info.md
@@ -125,6 +125,31 @@ keeps schedule identity generic and prevents a producer from hiding tile,
 layout, persistence, CTA, warp, stage, or other byte-affecting choices behind
 a process-local options object.
 
+`CanonicalSchedule` also has a standalone v1 identity. `serialize()` emits a
+three-field canonical MessagePack envelope, in lexical key order:
+
+| Key | V1 value |
+| --- | -------- |
+| `canonical_schedule_schema_version` | `1` |
+| `contract` | `pypto.canonical_schedule.v1` |
+| `resolved_schedule` | The eight-category map described above |
+
+`identity_digest` is the lowercase SHA-256 of that complete envelope.
+`deserialize()` accepts only exact canonical bytes and rejects malformed or
+trailing data, missing/duplicate/unknown/reordered fields, nonminimal scalar
+encodings, and unsupported schema or contract values. The envelope is capped
+at 1 MiB. Schema-shaped array, map, string, nesting, total-object, aggregate
+container-item, and binary-field limits are checked before MessagePack builds
+an object tree; binary, extension, and floating-point values are not part of
+this contract.
+
+The standalone envelope is not nested inside `KernelBuildSpec`.
+`KernelBuildSpec.resolved_schedule` retains the original bare eight-category
+body, byte for byte, so the existing KernelBuildSpec v1 wire format and digest
+remain unchanged. Conversely, standalone `CanonicalSchedule.deserialize()`
+rejects a bare body, and `KernelBuildSpec.deserialize()` rejects a standalone
+schedule envelope in its `resolved_schedule` field.
+
 ```python
 from pypto.compiler import (
     CanonicalSchedule,
@@ -148,6 +173,9 @@ resolved = CanonicalSchedule(
     stage=[u64("count", 3)],
     options=[ScheduleParameter("fast_math", ScheduleValueKind.Boolean, "false")],
 )
+schedule_wire_bytes = resolved.serialize()
+assert resolved.contract == "pypto.canonical_schedule.v1"
+assert CanonicalSchedule.deserialize(schedule_wire_bytes).serialize() == schedule_wire_bytes
 spec = KernelBuildSpec(
     source_ir_digest="1" * 64,
     callable_abi_digest="2" * 64,
